 "text": "Hi! How are you today? Sure. Si is the informal you when you' talking to one person you know well. It's like saying yo or man. Exactly. And ti is the formal you for talking to one person you don't know or an older person. That's also sit at home. It means the same thing but it' less informal and sounds nicer. That's a different story. Sir is used with a title, like when you address a knight as sir or a doctor as doctor. I' glad I could help. Just remember, sit is informal and ti is formal, and they change with age and situation.",
